te with","tags":["US","dialectal"]},{"word":"stallionize","source":"Thesaurus:copulate with"},{"word":"swive","source":"Thesaurus:copulate with","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"tap","source":"Thesaurus:copulate with"},{"word":"tup","source":"Thesaurus:copulate with"},{"word":"wap","source":"Thesaurus:copulate with"}],"raw_glosses":["(transitive, slang, originally US) To have sexual intercourse with."],"glosses":["To have sexual intercourse with."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"0c481790-44a5-4e4a-a084-d22c837e4e25"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"juicy":{"id":"90b8d9b6-9b80-4531-bb5a-4902bd0f7ceb","word":"juicy","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"containing juice","word":"suculento"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"exciting, interesting","word":"suculento"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"a juicy peach","bold_text_offsets":[[2,7]],"type":"example","id":"45eb9dfb-c3dc-4099-a2d1-ea169d5201ef"},{"text":"a juicy pot roast","bold_text_offsets":[[2,7]],"type":"example","id":"d93420fb-f232-41b4-812b-d52740933320"}],"links":[["juice","juice"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"sappy"},{"word":"succulent"},{"word":"succulous"}],"antonyms":[{"word":"dry"},{"word":"unjuicy"},{"word":";"},{"word":"dried"},{"word":"dried out"},{"word":"dried up"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"watery"},{"word":"oily"}],"glosses":["Having lots of juice."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"00f1cb1c-327f-46b4-b143-4c56b515c6a3"},{"examples":[{"text":"Near-synonyms: saucy, spicy","id":"3da76828-8beb-4820-9d9b-c337a0c3f923"},{"text":"I do not keep up with all the latest juicy rumors.","bold_text_offsets":[[37,42]],"type":"example","id":"982786e5-7892-4591-b45e-93ffe72d4d1b"},{"text":"I like getting my teeth into a nice juicy problem.","bold_text_offsets":[[36,41]],"type":"example","id":"61904e6e-fb6a-4d1e-9f9a-2d6df52c6112"},{"text":"If you’re looking for juicier confessions – that is, admissions of the kinds of sins unearthed on detective shows or reality TV – then you’ll want to look elsewhere. My sinning life is rather uneventful.","ref":"2014 November 12, James Martin, “Confessions of a Catholic priest”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[22,29]],"id":"794a9a54-96f1-47c8-b792-e9ec74d3ac02"},{"text":"Here are the five juiciest redactions from the Flynn sentencing document, with some context and a smidge of informed speculation about What It All Means.","ref":"2018 December 5, Chris Cillizza, “The 5 juiciest redactions in Michael Flynn’s sentencing document”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[18,26]],"id":"fad11a61-9562-48ad-a0ee-3a3721c8d705"},{"text":"“Gossip” is about a lot more than just juicy tidbits and the columnists that peddle them, presenting a multifaceted look at gossip’s role in the newspaper/media ecosystem and at Rupert Murdoch’s enterprises in particular.","ref":"2021 August 20, Brian Lowry, “‘Gossip’ charts how tabloid tattlers ‘escaped from their cages’ and rippled through the media”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[39,44]],"id":"d3713546-6048-4682-a206-cc7a5045a1d9"},{"text":"The former vice-president’s characterizations of peers such as Pete Buttigieg (talented but too gay for the America to accept as her running mate), and Josh Shapiro (an egoist) are not particularly juicy, but have already caused bad blood.","ref":"2025 September 22, Arwa Mahdawi, “107 Days by Kamala Harris review – no closure, no hope”, in The Guardian, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[198,203]],"id":"abc4060b-5d18-40ea-be5d-658d4aadd8d3"}],"links":[["story","story"],["Exciting","exciting#English"],["titillating","titillating"]],"antonyms":[{"word":"unjuicy"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"saucy"},{"word":"spicy"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"raw_glosses":["(figurative, of a story, etc.) Exciting; titillating."],"glosses":["Exciting; titillating."],"tags":["figurat